<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-05>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-05" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-22T08:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "Acknowledgement state mutated before peer delivery is attempted; failed peer delivery does not roll back local ack mutation" ;
  triage:description "write_mail_with_runtime calls acknowledgement.finish(...) -> mark_source_acknowledged as soon as the reply is durably persisted locally, inside MessageWriter::write -- which completes and returns before route_write invokes PostWriteRouter::dispatch to attempt HTTPS delivery to the remote peer. If delivery subsequently fails, mark_source_acknowledged has already committed and is never rolled back. The legacy ack_mail path lacks any router/rollback mechanism and calls write_mail_with_runtime directly without peer delivery gating." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs and any write path (including the legacy ack_mail path) that mutates acknowledgement state before/without confirming peer delivery success" ;
  triage:category "QA1" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T08:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-05/s11/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-05/s12/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-05/s13/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-05/s14/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-05/s15/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-05/s16/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s11/3642430d> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s12/a8ea0017> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s13/2adc5fa1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s14/ef0e5e2b> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s15/5a7a762f> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s16/1c23ac04> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s16/1c23ac04> ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAI-s16-offline-reconciliation" ;
  triage:highestFixedBranch "none" ;
  triage:correctionNote "2026-07-26 (quality-mgr): independently re-verified at integrate/phase-AI tip against arch-ctm's legacy close/waive batch recommendation -- still OPEN, not eligible for close/waive. crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs PreparedWrite::finish (line 282) is now correctly gated -- it is only invoked by PostWriteRouter::dispatch after peer delivery succeeds, per the doc comment at line 200: 'a peer-delivery error therefore leaves it pending.' However, crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs ack_mail_with_runtime (line 175) -- the CLI-facing legacy path exercised by `atm ack` -- still calls crate::send::write_mail_with_runtime directly (line 180), which persists and immediately calls .finish() with no router involvement and no peer-delivery gating. This is exactly the finding's original complaint ('the legacy ack_mail path lacks any router/rollback mechanism'). The router-gated daemon path is fixed; the legacy CLI path is not. Confirmed via direct code read, not self-report." .

